      "sha": "9a5e1ff947d4433ff5508b0fc0bfc0c0b9426c50",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-19T09:56:50.892Z",
      "commits": [
        {
          "sha": "9a5e1ff947d4433ff5508b0fc0bfc0c0b9426c50",
          "author_name": "Brandon Fryslie",
          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-19T09:55:44Z",
          "message": "Merge e656ae2280cbfbf0a220d1f253ccf6ab47e34fde into 664f8da27681e8e52d2e98d26bbd7dd358214e5e\n"
        },
        {
          "sha": "e656ae2280cbfbf0a220d1f253ccf6ab47e34fde",
          "author_name": "Brandon Fryslie",
          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-19T02:55:29-07:00",
          "message": "fix(test): a test daemon runs on the arguments the client ships, and its signal is named for what it reaches (f6eo)\n\nThe source entry resolves tsx's loader through the package's exports and puts\nit in front of the client's own daemon arguments, heap cap included. Because\nthe client refuses to spawn on a malformed memory budget, the tests of the\ndaemon's own refusal run it by hand. killTree becomes signalDaemon.\n"
        },
        {
          "sha": "a19ec2b1c69b3c896acfca239817b62ce6900f64",
          "author_name": "Brandon Fryslie",
          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-19T02:38:14-07:00",
          "message": "fix(test): a test daemon is node itself, so the signal that stops it reaches its shutdown (f6eo)\n\nThe tsx CLI relays a signal to a worker of its own and SIGKILLs that worker\nif it has not answered within ~60 ms, so on a loaded runner a daemon stopped\nwith SIGTERM died before its handler restored tmux or released the registry.\nEvery process-tier daemon now runs as node with tsx's loader imported, through\nthe one spawn helper, so the pid a test holds and signals is the daemon's own.\nThe tmux-restore test adds the case that freezes the daemon across the\nSIGTERM.\n"
        }
      ]
    },
